                    We are developing HappyMat(TM) Prototype #1, a smart interactive doormat incorporating sensors, a digital display, addressable LED lighting, wireless connectivity, camera/audio components, embedded electronics, and a custom physical structure.



We are seeking an experienced Lead Mechatronics / Product Development Engineer to serve as the technical lead and primary system integrator. You will collaborate with other HappyMat specialists, including embedded/firmware, mechanical/CAD, prototype fabrication/electronics, and IoT/interface development.



Primary Responsibilities:



Define the overall prototype architecture.

Coordinate technical decisions across the engineering team.

Integrate sensors, display, LED lighting, camera/audio, controller, wireless connectivity, and mechanical components.

Coordinate technical integration with the other HappyMat team members.

Help select practical off-the-shelf modules where they reduce cost and development time.

Lead troubleshooting and integration testing.

Lead the final functional demonstration.

Deliver applicable engineering files and documentation.



Preferred Skills / Experience:

Mechatronics;

Product Development;

Embedded Electronics;

Sensors;

ESP32/MCU Systems;

Displays;

Addressable LEDs;

Wi-Fi/Bluetooth;

Camera/Audio Integration;

Troubleshooting;

Hands-On Prototyping



How to Apply:



Begin your proposal with HAPPYMAT.



Describe one physical product or functional prototype you personally helped build. Explain exactly what you contributed and provide photos or video if available.

Please include your rate for the complete assigned scope.

NDA required before confidential HappyMat technical information is shared.



Teamwork requirement: The selected professional must communicate reliably with the other HappyMat team members, participate in integration and testing as applicable, and deliver all project-specific work files associated with the assigned role.
